<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Perfume Pagoda by Motorbike: Luggage Packing Guide</h1>
<p>Luggage for the Perfume Pagoda ride is not a packing problem, it is a custody problem, because the day travels in three modes, road, river and foot, and everything you carry must be prepared to change vehicles with you. The corridor takes the machine south, the water takes the passenger on, and the stone steps take only what the legs agree to carry. Pack for all three masters at once, and the luggage stops being luggage and becomes the trip&rsquo;s quiet companion, as this guide explains without inventing a single weather forecast or timetable.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk audits every bag before the southern pilgrimage. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, absorb the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
